      <div class="column is-two-fifths bio">
        <h1 class="title is-4 is-uppercase">About</h1>
         <p>
          Hello! I’m Elliot, a design leader with over 15 years of agency experience. I’ve built my career across categories from hospitality to fashion to automotive, Broadway to the Super Bowl. The joy has always been in taking individual pieces, ideas, people, and details, and fitting them together into something greater than the sum of their parts. I was taught to sweat the small stuff and do it yourself whenever possible, and that mindset has stuck with me.
<br><br>
As my role has evolved, I now focus on team leadership, client management, and design thinking. At Wasserman, I built the in-house design studio from the ground up. What started as a team of zero is now 18 multidisciplinary designers. My job is to empower people, creating an environment that fosters both creative discipline and imagination. A space where designers can focus on doing great work and growing personally, knowing they’re supported.
<br><br>
Beyond leadership, I remain hands-on. I’ve collaborated closely with creative directors to concept, create, and push design forward for brands like Red Bull, Progressive, Molson Coors, Ferrari, AT&T, Jack Daniel’s, and American Express. These projects haven’t just delivered results; they’ve reimagined how these brands show up in global culture, from large-scale experiential activations to intimate brand moments.
         <br>
         
         </p>
